  "title": "review: S1f env_policy: allowlisted environment propagation for worker subprocesses (off/shadow/active), names-only shadow log, never a secret value (P22)",
  "spec": "Create orchestrator/env_policy.py. worker_env(role, *, base, extra, cfg) -> (env, stripped): base is the parent environment mapping, extra the keys the caller must set (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, ORCH_TASK_ID, oauth token env for the account, resolved [secrets.<role>] keys), cfg the pool config. Config in .orchestrator/pool.toml [secrets]: env_mode = \"shadow\" (values off, shadow, active; add with a dated comment) and env_passthrough = [\"PATH\",\"HOME\",\"USER\",\"LOGNAME\",\"LANG\",\"LC_ALL\",\"TERM\",\"SHELL\",\"TMPDIR\",\"XDG_*\",\"CLAUDE_*\",\"ORCH_*\",\"UV_*\",\"VIRTUAL_ENV\",\"PYTHONPATH\",\"NODE_*\",\"GIT_*\",\"SSH_AUTH_SOCK\"] (glob patterns; defaults used when absent). Rules: active -> env contains only base keys matching the passthrough patterns plus every extra key; shadow -> env is base plus extra unchanged, but stripped lists the keys active would have removed; off -> no computation, stripped empty. Keys whose name contains KEY, TOKEN, SECRET, PASSWORD, PASSWD, CREDENTIAL or AUTH are never passed through by pattern in active mode unless named exactly in extra or listed in [secrets.<role>] (so CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN reaches the worker only because spawn passes it as extra). Shadow and active both log one runs row via bus.log_run(role=\"env_policy\", task=..., outcome=mode, stripped=<sorted key names>, count=n) \u2014 key names only, never values; the row must never raise.\nWire: spawn.py where the claude -p env is built (around line 1020-1025) and executor.py where codex exec subprocesses get their environment (find the subprocess call; if it inherits os.environ implicitly, pass env explicitly). Also audit and document (docs/hermes-hardening/06-credential-filtering.md): which env keys the current machine would strip in active mode (names only, measured by running worker_env against os.environ in shadow and listing the names), where jev.redact already applies, and that logs never carry values. Do not change [secrets.<role>] resolution. Test fixtures use synthetic names and values that are not credential-shaped.\nSpec review T-1089 folded in: (1) The credential-name veto matches whole underscore-separated name tokens (KEY, TOKEN, SECRET, PASSWORD, PASSWD, CREDENTIAL, CREDENTIALS, AUTH), so GIT_AUTHOR_NAME (token AUTHOR) passes; an env_passthrough entry that is an exact name (no wildcard) overrides the veto, which is how the default SSH_AUTH_SOCK survives; glob entries never override it. (2) worker_env(role, *, base, extra, cfg, task_id=None): the runs row uses task_id; spawn passes the task id, executor passes task_id, goals/planner_shadow pass the goal or launch id. (3) Scope adds orchestrator/goals.py (_create_goal_task and launch_planner claude -p environments) and orchestrator/planner_shadow.py (launch): every claude -p or codex exec environment the orchestrator builds goes through worker_env, so the audit doc covers all spawn paths (list them). (4) executor.py: role execute, extra = ORCH_TASK_ID plus the resolved [secrets.execute] keys when that table exists, plus CODEX_HOME and HOME when set (codex reads its auth from there); shadow first, and the doc lists (names only) what active mode would strip from the codex environment on this machine so the human decides the flip.\nSpec review T-1111 folded in: (1) extra is whatever the caller computes per call and always wins over base: goals._create_goal_task passes ORCH_ROOT and ORCH_GOAL_TEXT, launch_planner passes ORCH_ROOT, planner_shadow.launch passes ORCH_ROOT and ORCH_SHADOW, spawn passes CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, ORCH_TASK_ID and the oauth token env, executor passes ORCH_TASK_ID, CODEX_HOME and HOME; the passthrough glob only decides which BASE keys survive. Test: a caller-supplied ORCH_ROOT replaces a stale base value in every mode. (2) TOML: the new [secrets] header with env_mode and env_passthrough is inserted ABOVE the existing [secrets.scout] block (a table's own keys must precede its dotted subtables), with a comment; verify the file still parses with tomllib in the test suite.\nRepository rules: unittest (not pytest), tests/_harness.py single ORCH_ROOT fixture; every acceptance test id tests/test_<module>.py::test_name is a method def test_name(self) in a unittest.TestCase. No new third-party dependencies. Never write secret values to any file or log. Do not quote template placeholder tokens (double braces) anywhere in code comments or docs. Run .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh . until green; the base suite must stay green. Do not ask questions: decide, and note decisions in the result summary. Read docs/context-economy/00-overview.md only if you need the evidence/decision_log conventions.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1114"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_env_policy.py::test_active_mode_allowlists_and_keeps_extra (a base env with secret-looking names is stripped, PATH and ORCH_* kept, extra keys kept)",
    "tests/test_env_policy.py::test_shadow_mode_only_reports (env unchanged, stripped names listed, log row written with names only)",
    "tests/test_env_policy.py::test_off_mode_noop",
    "tests/test_env_policy.py::test_log_row_never_contains_values (a synthetic value never appears in the runs row)",
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_spawn_uses_env_policy (patched Popen receives the env from worker_env; oauth token passed as extra)",
    "tests/test_env_policy.py::test_token_veto_and_exact_name_override (GIT_AUTHOR_NAME passes, SSH_AUTH_SOCK passes via exact entry, a name with the token TOKEN is stripped)",
    "tests/test_env_policy.py::test_all_spawn_paths_use_worker_env (spawn, executor, goals, planner_shadow patched launches receive worker_env output)",
    "tests/test_env_policy.py::test_extra_always_overrides_base_and_pool_toml_parses",
