    {
      "ts": 1790167278.727503,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "Implementation otherwise matches the spec closely: worker_env's active/shadow/off semantics, the credential-token veto with exact-name/role-secret override (verified against test_token_veto_and_exact_name_override's GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/SSH_AUTH_SOCK/glob cases), extra-always-wins-over-base, task_id plumbing, the pool.toml [secrets] table placed above [secrets.scout], and all five spawn paths (spawn.run_claude, executor._run, goals._create_goal_task, goals.launch_planner, planner_shadow.launch) wired through worker_env with matching audit documentation in docs/hermes-hardening/06-credential-filtering.md. The one substantive issue is that wiring env_policy into goals.py reintroduces exactly the ROOT/STATE/bus coupling that module's own import-boundary comment (and its prior design, which routed all bus access through a repo_path-scoped subprocess) was written to prevent -- a real regression of a documented invariant, low blast radius (telemetry only, no crash, no value leakage) but untested and worth a decision before merge rather than silent acceptance.",
        "verdict": "request_changes",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/goals.py",
            "line": 119,
            "issue": "_create_goal_task and launch_planner now call env_policy.worker_env() directly in-process, and worker_env calls bus.log_run() internally. bus.log_run() writes to RUNS = STATE/\"runs\"/<date>.jsonl where STATE = ROOT / \".orchestrator\", and ROOT/STATE are module-level constants resolved once from this process's own ORCH_ROOT env var (orchestrator/__init__.py), not from the repo_path argument goals.py receives. This breaks the invariant stated in goals.py's own docstring (updated by this same diff to whitelist env_policy without addressing the conflict): 'It never calls Pool(), never calls any other bus.*/spawn.* function, and never references orchestrator.ROOT/STATE. Every path it touches derives from the realpath'd repo_path argument, so the same code works against this repo or any target repo scaffolded by install.install.' Before this diff, goals.py only ever touched bus/ROOT/STATE inside the isolated SCRIPT subprocess (uv run --project PACKAGE_REPO python -), which explicitly sets its own ORCH_ROOT=str(repo_path) for that child process. The new call bypasses that isolation: when goals.py manages a goal/Planner launch against a target repo other than this orchestrator's own root, the env_policy runs row is written into (or silently dropped from, since log_run failures are swallowed) the wrong orchestrator's own runs log rather than the target repo's. No test catches this because test_all_spawn_paths_use_worker_env mocks env_policy.worker_env outright, so the real bus.log_run codepath triggered from goals.py is never exercised.",
            "severity": "med"
          }
        ],
        "packet_version": "d99c85023faf",
        "confidence": 0.0,
        "provenance": [
          "repo"
        ]
      }
